A||||8||beer_stud_21||Subdividing the topics on PFF||||3||
Z||000000||beer_stud_21||09-03-2001||07:58 PM||||Hey Cliff.  What do you think about the idea of breaking down the topics a bit further.  Before I got into fieros I read a forum about T-birds.  Thats where I got the idea from.  I really like how that forum is divided up.  You can see that forum  <A HREF="http://pub5.ezboard.com/bfoxthunderbirds.html" TARGET=_blank>here</A>.  I think it would make the forum a lot nicer to read and above all would keep topics at the top of their respective sections for a longer amount of time.  It would allow people to see a topic longer before it got pushed off the first page.  Technical could be divided up something like this::<P><B>2.5l "Iron Duke"</B><BR><B>2.8l V6</B><BR><B>Engine Swaps</B> (Because there are so many engine swaps for fieros this could be broken down even further)<BR><B>Drivetrain</B> (Since you would not want to fragment these sort of questions across the various engine sections.)<BR><B>Body Modifications</B> (For all the scoop info, rebodys, spoilers, tail light mods etc.  Could also include paint and tires..<BR><B>Suspension/Steering</B> (Brakes, Steering, Lowering Mods etc.)<BR>Then there could be some kind of general technical section that would be the catch all for other technical info and questions.  For example:  Stereo questions or front mount battery mods etc.)<P>I think general chat could be divided up a bit too.  There is a lot of stuff that goes through general, and for the same reasons as technical I think it would be benificial to divide it up to allow topics to stay at the top for longer.  Any suggestions on what some possible catagories could be?  A "readers rides" section could be cool.  A place where anyone that wanted to could create one topic to post pics and talk about their car.  They could simply edit the post when they wanted to update info or pictures.  <P>Well, I guess thats it.  What do you think Cliff?  Or anyone else for that matter?<P>-marlin<P>||||reg||3
