Z||000005||gargoyle||09-03-2001||08:46 PM||||Sorry beer_stud but I think it works pretty good as is. This way you scan down thru the topics and if you see one that catches your interest you read it. It easy enough to go to the next page. Well that's my three cents for what it's worth.<P>Ok, maybe a new section for picture posts, but wait, we have the gallery, isn't that what that is for??<p>[This message has been edited by gargoyle (edited 09-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||09-03-2001||08:58 PM||||I think dividing sections would confuse too many people. Posts get in the wrong sections already, just imagine what would happen if we gave people 10 more choices on where to post.||||reg||1
Z||000007||beer_stud_21||09-03-2001||10:03 PM||||Ouch.. hehe.  Looks like I'm gettin blown out of the water here.  The reason the additional sections are good is because there are less posts in each one.  Less posts mean the stuff that does get posted gets seen for longer.  Besides for example:  A V6 owner (since there are some duke hating V6 owners on here) would be able to jump straight to the V6 section.  Which would be filled with V6 related questions and info.  Then when you want to post a question about how to time your V6 your post wont be pushed down to the second page within a few hours by all the posts asking about scoops, tires, rims, paint, iron dukes, etc etc etc.  Besides some people come here just to find info about a certain aspect of their car.  So there is no need to search through the entire technical section if you only want info on a specific thing.  This is especially important for people who don't read the forum on a daily basis.  With everything combined someone who reads the forum once a week would miss a lot of posts that might have info they would be interested in unless they dig through the first few pages.<P>Well, it makes sense to me, but I guess I will just go over in the corner and pout and feel sorry for myself...  Or maybe I'll go hang out with Songman!  hehe   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
